<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Red Guards (Finland)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-guards-russia">Red Guards</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> were armed militias of workers formed by the labour movement in 1917, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-revolution">Russian Revolution</a> had removed the old order. In January 1918 they seized Helsinki and the industrial south, starting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finnish-civil-war">Finnish Civil War</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-movement">White Guards</a>. Poorly trained and led, they were defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tampere">Tampere</a> and elsewhere by May 1918, and thousands of their members died in executions and prison camps.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/red-guards-finland.jpg" alt="Red Guards (Finland)" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julius Jääskeläinen · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_Guards_and_Russians_fighting_on_the_red_side_in_Ruovesi,_Pirkanmaa,_Finland,_1918._(50213249403).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
